  "findings": {
    "not_structural": "Tested the hypothesis that the 97% alert rate had a structural cause like the Layer-1 IQR collapse. It does not. The per-class rate normalisation IS a defect and is fixed, but at 47.6% prevalence it only inflates 5:1 to 5.5:1 and moves the threshold 0.1282 -> 0.1627 (PPR 0.970 -> 0.954).",
    "actual_cause": "The asserted 5:1 cost ratio does all the work. For a calibrated model the optimum is c_fp/(c_fp+c_fn) = 0.167, and 95.4% of predicted probabilities exceed it because the model's outputs concentrate near the 47.6% base rate (p5=0.20, p25=0.36). The threshold is CORRECT for 5:1; the alert volume is what an optimal 5:1 rule does on this distribution.",
    "rate_form_becomes_serious_under_the_new_target": "At the <30 prevalence of 11.16% the same rate-form defect inflates 5:1 into an effective 39.8:1. Fixed before the target switch rather than after."
  },
